  "info": {
    "lines": [
      "<p>This song uses a custom Palette stylesheet, called <i>light</i>.  Unlike <i>CycleOfColors</i>, it comprises yellows to show all notes except those in the major triad which use yellowy greens.</p>",
      "",
      "<p>The song then transposes chromatically through all twelve semitones, showing how the diatonic pattern shifts up the neck, preserving the basic shape on a P4 tuning, so you can see how the pattern is the same regardless of what key you are playing in.  It then becomes an excercise in knowing which frets have roots, or some other way to anchor your pattern to the neck during transposition.</p>",
      "",
      "<p>See also: <a href=\"?song=theory/mode-nat-minor-transposed.json\">mode-nat-minor-transposed.json</a> where we repeat the same excercise with a blue Palatte stylesheet for minor moods.</p>"
    ]
  },
